CloudBurrow patch 93 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1783). Applies after patch 0090.

A JSON value bound as its text inside a STRUCT or an ARRAY was cast to
JSON by quoting it: StringValue.ToJSON is the string's JSON encoding. The
emulator binds a tabledata.insertAll or load row's RECORD as a map whose
JSON field is the client's JSON text, so a stored STRUCT<d JSON> kept d as
a JSON string: TO_JSON_STRING(s.d) was "\"{\\\"x\\\":1}\"", JSON_VALUE(s.d,
'$.x') NULL, and an object table's ref.details (an ObjectRef's JSON) could
not be read as JSON. BigQuery has no cast or coercion from STRING to JSON
in SQL, so a STRING reaching a cast to JSON is a bound value: valid JSON
text is now read as the JSON it is, at any depth (STRUCT fields, ARRAY
elements, ARRAY<STRUCT> fields). Text that is not JSON stays a JSON
string, as before. struct_json_field_test.go fails without the patch and
passes with it.

